fix(touch): the touch part is a Synaptics S3908 at 0x4B, not an S6SY761 at 0x48

The kebab vendor DTB (decompiled from the kebab image kept on the build
host) has two mutually exclusive touch nodes under i2c@a94000:

  sec-s6sy761@48      reg 0x48, chip-name SY771, project-name 19821,
                      panel = <generic Samsung, ANA6705, ANA6706, DD305>
  synaptics-s3908@4B  reg 0x4B, chip-name S3908, project-name 19805,
                      panel = <BOE, DD305, AMB655X>

This unit's panel is the Samsung AMB655X, and that phandle appears only in
the S3908 list; the DTB's own bootargs also carry project_name=19805.  The
earlier note that took the first node for the board was wrong.

Change KT_I2C_ADDR to 0x4B, retitle the driver and its boot banner, and
rewrite the two comments that justified the old address and the old
"vendor uses Samsung sec_ts" claim: the vendor drives this node with its
Synaptics TCM-style driver, so the command family already matches and the
open question is the firmware's exact opcode set, not the protocol family.

No I/O behaviour changes beyond the slave address.

